  "$comment": "Symbol glyphs for the terminal view (WEB-58), cut from Nerd Fonts Symbols Only 3.4.0 (SymbolsNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf in the release zip below) with fonttools 4.55.3: pyftsubset --unicodes=<range> --no-hinting --desubroutinize, then the name table set to 'termocode symbols' (no reserved font name is used) and saved as woff2. One file per glyph set: the browser fetches a file only when a terminal row shows a glyph of its range. Never edit a file here; to update, cut new files and change the rows (sha384 of each file). cmd/webbuild checks every hash and copies LICENSE.txt into licenses.txt.",
